1
00:01:32,710 --> 00:01:34,979
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:37,710
[Episode 19]

3
00:01:38,710 --> 00:01:40,509
It wasn't Yu Sanhua who died.

4
00:01:41,590 --> 00:01:43,150
So who was that body in the river?

5
00:01:43,150 --> 00:01:44,350
Who cares who she was?

6
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:46,110
The point is, she wasn't Yu Sanhua.

7
00:01:46,110 --> 00:01:48,039
Now we should think about
what we should do.

8
00:01:48,039 --> 00:01:49,000
What do we do?

9
00:01:49,479 --> 00:01:51,280
Exonerate Qian Xingliang immediately!

10
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:52,479
Keep your voice down.

11
00:01:54,229 --> 00:01:54,759
No.

12
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,120
He's done eight years for nothing.

13
00:01:57,590 --> 00:01:59,640
Luckily he wasn't executed back then.

14
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:00,560
Otherwise,

15
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:04,750
the consequences would be unimaginable.

16
00:02:07,510 --> 00:02:09,110
It's a relief in misfortune.

17
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:10,039
Relief?

18
00:02:10,870 --> 00:02:12,030
What should we do?

19
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:13,740
Someone has to

20
00:02:13,770 --> 00:02:15,180
take the blame for this.

21
00:02:15,610 --> 00:02:16,800
Best case, we get disciplined;

22
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:18,329
worst case, we're both out.

23
00:02:21,430 --> 00:02:22,280
I've wasted over 30 years

24
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:23,810
of my life through all those campaigns.

25
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:25,540
I finally got back on the bench,

26
00:02:25,850 --> 00:02:27,460
but I've never been given any big cases.

27
00:02:27,460 --> 00:02:28,730
Then I finally get one,

28
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:30,610
and it turns into this disaster.

29
00:02:38,810 --> 00:02:39,530
Ms. Mei,

30
00:02:40,690 --> 00:02:41,340
if

31
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:43,460
only

32
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:44,680
we'd pushed harder back then.

33
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:45,930
That's obvious.

34
00:02:52,850 --> 00:02:54,620
T-That's not what I meant.

35
00:02:54,850 --> 00:02:55,570
I admit

36
00:02:56,060 --> 00:02:58,380
you did insist on suspending the trial

37
00:02:58,460 --> 00:02:59,530
and returning the file.

38
00:02:59,530 --> 00:03:00,250
But I

39
00:03:00,390 --> 00:03:01,590
reported everything
to the Adjudication Committee

40
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:02,190
as well.

41
00:03:02,730 --> 00:03:04,780
In the end, it was the committee
that decided on

42
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:05,740
the death penalty.

43
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:06,900
If it were up to them,

44
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:09,580
Qian Xingliang
would've been shot long ago.

45
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:10,820
Now they find out it's wrong

46
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:11,940
and there's a mistake,

47
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:13,460
and they want us to be the scapegoats.

48
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:14,620
Does that seem fair?

49
00:03:14,970 --> 00:03:16,060
Easy now.

50
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:18,380
Let's not

51
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:19,500
overthink it.

52
00:03:20,430 --> 00:03:21,710
The court's decision

53
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:23,380
won't come down

54
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:24,130
for a while,

55
00:03:25,810 --> 00:03:26,380
right?

56
00:03:31,010 --> 00:03:31,690
Xia,

57
00:03:32,410 --> 00:03:33,060
can you

58
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:35,500
get in touch with Chief Judge Yu?

59
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:37,500
He's your school fellow.

60
00:03:37,660 --> 00:03:39,190
He'll definitely help you.

61
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:41,120
And helping you is helping me.

62
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:42,880
I really can't take this fall.

63
00:03:43,730 --> 00:03:45,460
I can't afford to lose this job.

64
00:03:47,130 --> 00:03:47,690
Xia,

65
00:03:48,250 --> 00:03:49,220
I'm begging you.

66
00:03:49,810 --> 00:03:51,150
Please help me.

67
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:52,410
It was all my fault.

68
00:03:52,810 --> 00:03:53,660
Please,

69
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:55,770
just help me.

70
00:03:56,540 --> 00:03:57,500
Help me, okay?

71
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:02,570
Xia.

72
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:07,920
Thank you for trusting me,
Court Pres. Qiu.

73
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:08,880
I'll get it done.

74
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:10,270
Don't worry.

75
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:15,760
No problem.

76
00:04:16,329 --> 00:04:17,170
Court Pres. Qiu,

77
00:04:17,170 --> 00:04:18,260
I have some other work to wrap up.

78
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:19,720
I'll get back to you later.

79
00:04:20,899 --> 00:04:21,300
Okay.

80
00:04:21,779 --> 00:04:22,290
Bye.

81
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:24,260
Come in.

82
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:32,040
You've never been to my office, have you?

83
00:04:35,490 --> 00:04:36,930
Judge Xia, you're always too busy,

84
00:04:36,930 --> 00:04:39,130
and I never had the chance to invite you.

85
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:40,420
Have a seat.

86
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:44,500
What's up?

87
00:04:47,030 --> 00:04:47,890
Chief Judge Yu,

88
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:49,280
there's something

89
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:50,470
I need to report.

90
00:04:50,470 --> 00:04:51,409
Chief Judge Yu?

91
00:04:51,409 --> 00:04:52,810
Are you trying to mock me?

92
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:58,060
Let me tell you, Comrade Xia,

93
00:04:58,340 --> 00:04:59,100
if one day

94
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:00,220
I actually become

95
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:01,480
the President
of the Supreme People's Court,

96
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:02,310
you won't get to call me

97
00:05:02,310 --> 00:05:03,640
by my full name anymore.

98
00:05:07,850 --> 00:05:08,460
Fine.

99
00:05:09,050 --> 00:05:09,710
Yu Gaoyuan.

100
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:11,630
Go ahead.

101
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:15,820
You must already know
about Yu Sanhua being alive-

102
00:05:27,370 --> 00:05:28,640
So that's what you meant

103
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:29,940
when you told me in the cafeteria
just now to push the responsibility

104
00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:31,220
onto the Adjudication Committee?

105
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:32,570
I was afraid they'd come straight to you,

106
00:05:32,570 --> 00:05:34,659
and I wouldn't have
a chance to work things out.

107
00:05:34,659 --> 00:05:36,050
Just now, Court Pres. Qiu called me

108
00:05:36,050 --> 00:05:36,820
and said he's putting me

109
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:37,659
in charge of this.

110
00:05:37,659 --> 00:05:39,390
That makes things a lot easier.

111
00:05:42,870 --> 00:05:44,020
I remember it very clearly.

112
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:45,480
You were the one who pushed

113
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:46,990
to suspend the trial

114
00:05:46,990 --> 00:05:50,190
and send the file back
for further investigation, right?

115
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,100
Then you're fine.

116
00:05:52,530 --> 00:05:53,900
Even if the whole court gets blamed,

117
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:54,940
it won't fall on you.

118
00:05:54,940 --> 00:05:56,870
They should actually commend you.

119
00:06:00,050 --> 00:06:00,580
No,

120
00:06:01,390 --> 00:06:02,720
that's not why I'm here.

121
00:06:04,050 --> 00:06:04,850
Besides, I can't say

122
00:06:04,850 --> 00:06:05,940
I have no responsibility.

123
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:06,890
If I'd been

124
00:06:06,910 --> 00:06:07,670
more persistent,

125
00:06:07,670 --> 00:06:08,480
stuck to my guns,

126
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:11,140
maybe things
would've turned out differently.

127
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:12,260
I just think

128
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:14,130
this needs to be set straight.

129
00:06:14,860 --> 00:06:17,190
Judge Mei and I will take responsibility,

130
00:06:17,650 --> 00:06:19,580
but only for the part
that is truly ours to bear.

131
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:21,980
Our Adjudication Committee
recommended the death penalty.

132
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:23,860
The Provincial High Court reviewed it
and commuted it to a reprieve.

133
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:25,140
They're both responsible.

134
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:26,290
Why do you insist on

135
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:27,680
being tied to Mei Fang?

136
00:06:30,090 --> 00:06:31,840
Your proposal
to return the case for retrial

137
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:32,750
is on the record.

138
00:06:32,750 --> 00:06:34,130
Mei Fang was the one
who handed down the death sentence.

139
00:06:34,130 --> 00:06:35,050
But she just read

140
00:06:35,050 --> 00:06:36,050
the Adjudication Committee's decision.

141
00:06:36,050 --> 00:06:37,310
This is a big issue now.

142
00:06:39,850 --> 00:06:41,530
The tri-department meeting's
already happened.

143
00:06:41,530 --> 00:06:43,409
The police, the prosecutor, the court—
everyone's gonna be affected.

144
00:06:43,409 --> 00:06:44,409
You'd be lucky to walk away

145
00:06:44,409 --> 00:06:44,930
clean yourself,

146
00:06:44,930 --> 00:06:46,860
and you're trying to save Mei Fang?

147
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:55,050
Listen to me, don't do anything reckless.

148
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:09,300
I've written it all down.

149
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,430
That should be okay.

150
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:13,040
Reporting, Qian Xingliang is here.

151
00:07:14,130 --> 00:07:15,060
Come in, please.

152
00:07:26,370 --> 00:07:27,300
Qian Xingliang,

153
00:07:27,460 --> 00:07:28,220
have a seat.

154
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:31,000
Sir, I'm fine.

155
00:07:34,210 --> 00:07:35,140
Qian Xingliang.

156
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:36,159
Come on.

157
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:38,409
Just have a seat.

158
00:07:41,780 --> 00:07:42,100
Sit.

159
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:47,130
Qian Xingliang,

160
00:07:47,970 --> 00:07:49,200
we're bringing you in today

161
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:50,020
because we have

162
00:07:50,020 --> 00:07:50,950
some questions.

163
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:52,920
You need to answer honestly.

164
00:07:53,210 --> 00:07:53,890
Yes, sir.

165
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:58,170
Back then,

166
00:07:58,420 --> 00:08:00,060
why did you confess?

167
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:05,970
What?

168
00:08:07,590 --> 00:08:08,460
In other words,

169
00:08:08,530 --> 00:08:09,480
how did you admit

170
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:10,750
you killed Yu Sanhua?

171
00:08:13,570 --> 00:08:14,250
Sir,

172
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:16,080
I confessed. I accept my sentence,

173
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:18,210
I'm reforming myself, starting over.

174
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:20,170
Sit down.

175
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,480
I'm ordering you to sit.

176
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:32,530
How did you give that

177
00:08:32,549 --> 00:08:33,799
confession back then?

178
00:08:33,799 --> 00:08:34,770
Tell us about it.

179
00:08:35,370 --> 00:08:36,200
Be honest.

180
00:08:38,130 --> 00:08:38,820
Sir,

181
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:40,490
I've already confessed.

182
00:08:40,490 --> 00:08:41,890
I've been behaving well.

183
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:44,970
I've earned over eighty points this year.

184
00:08:45,230 --> 00:08:46,510
If I get to a hundred,

185
00:08:46,970 --> 00:08:47,340
I...

186
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:50,600
I can get another t-three months off.

187
00:08:52,850 --> 00:08:53,740
Qian Xingliang,

188
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:54,820
you didn't kill her.

189
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:55,540
So why did you say

190
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:56,540
you did?

191
00:09:01,470 --> 00:09:03,230
We want to know the truth.

192
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:09,510
Sir.

193
00:09:13,220 --> 00:09:14,130
What did you...

194
00:09:15,970 --> 00:09:16,850
just say?

195
00:09:20,180 --> 00:09:21,100
You know

196
00:09:22,220 --> 00:09:24,020
I didn't do it?

197
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:26,390
Sir.

198
00:09:28,250 --> 00:09:31,400
I'm innocent. I didn't do it.

199
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:36,610
Qian Xingliang.

200
00:09:37,850 --> 00:09:38,710
Come on, get up.

201
00:09:50,370 --> 00:09:51,340
In the second part,

202
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:53,010
we've fully demonstrated

203
00:09:53,010 --> 00:09:54,180
the necessity of

204
00:09:54,180 --> 00:09:55,700
"innocent until proven guilty"

205
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:56,620
in judicial practice.

206
00:09:56,620 --> 00:09:58,100
When the evidence in a case

207
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:59,970
can't be solid and complete,

208
00:10:00,010 --> 00:10:01,810
or form a full chain of evidence,

209
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:03,130
and reasonable doubt

210
00:10:03,130 --> 00:10:04,340
can't be ruled out,

211
00:10:04,830 --> 00:10:05,490
the benefit

212
00:10:05,770 --> 00:10:07,300
should go to the defendant.

213
00:10:07,610 --> 00:10:08,730
Judicial authorities should act

214
00:10:08,730 --> 00:10:11,940
in accordance with the principle
of "innocent until proven guilty."

215
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:12,580
Cheng,

216
00:10:13,940 --> 00:10:15,070
didn't he always say

217
00:10:15,140 --> 00:10:16,330
his doctoral dissertation

218
00:10:16,330 --> 00:10:18,530
was going to be about the death penalty?

219
00:10:19,340 --> 00:10:20,940
His views

220
00:10:20,970 --> 00:10:22,180
have shifted a bit.

221
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:24,610
He feels the death penalty

222
00:10:24,630 --> 00:10:25,830
is too broad a topic,

223
00:10:26,350 --> 00:10:28,220
and that promoting
"innocent until proven guilty"

224
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,610
is the real driving force

225
00:10:29,610 --> 00:10:31,210
in the current environment.

226
00:10:32,060 --> 00:10:34,070
The fear of letting
one guilty person go free.

227
00:10:34,070 --> 00:10:35,190
That's exactly how

228
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:36,280
we've ended up with

229
00:10:36,540 --> 00:10:38,270
so many wrongful convictions.

230
00:10:38,730 --> 00:10:40,540
I've noticed a few

231
00:10:40,540 --> 00:10:42,060
cases you cited

232
00:10:42,060 --> 00:10:44,060
in your paper where guilt

233
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:45,420
was presumed instead

234
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:47,250
and they're all from

235
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:48,740
quite early on.

236
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:50,850
Yes, most of them

237
00:10:50,850 --> 00:10:52,490
occurred in the early years

238
00:10:52,510 --> 00:10:53,970
of reform and opening-up.

239
00:10:54,180 --> 00:10:56,480
Well, since your case

240
00:10:56,510 --> 00:10:58,270
examples are all from that

241
00:10:58,390 --> 00:11:00,050
specific historical period,

242
00:11:00,770 --> 00:11:02,130
you need to provide

243
00:11:02,130 --> 00:11:04,180
a fuller discussion of the causes

244
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:07,010
and the necessity behind them.

245
00:11:11,100 --> 00:11:12,610
Is that really necessary?

246
00:11:13,370 --> 00:11:14,490
Absolutely.

247
00:11:15,010 --> 00:11:15,850
Why did China

248
00:11:15,850 --> 00:11:17,770
launch several severe crackdowns

249
00:11:17,770 --> 00:11:19,250
on crime in the 1980s?

250
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:21,540
There were deep practical

251
00:11:22,130 --> 00:11:23,420
and social reasons.

252
00:11:23,770 --> 00:11:24,340
In the early days

253
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:25,800
of reform and opening-up,

254
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:28,260
from a social management perspective,

255
00:11:28,820 --> 00:11:29,850
those measures

256
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:32,340
quickly stabilized public order

257
00:11:32,690 --> 00:11:34,340
and provided

258
00:11:34,340 --> 00:11:35,400
a safe environment

259
00:11:35,540 --> 00:11:37,540
for reform.

260
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:38,970
But now,

261
00:11:39,750 --> 00:11:41,970
the historical mission of these policies

262
00:11:41,970 --> 00:11:43,180
has been completed.

263
00:11:43,870 --> 00:11:45,670
The importance of the rule of law

264
00:11:45,710 --> 00:11:47,520
has taken deeper root.

265
00:11:48,670 --> 00:11:49,150
And

266
00:11:49,270 --> 00:11:51,540
of course, I agree with you.

267
00:11:51,930 --> 00:11:54,180
Now is the right time to further refine

268
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:55,590
for more than ten years.

269
00:11:56,250 --> 00:11:58,100
for over a decade.

270
00:12:06,670 --> 00:12:09,010
Let's celebrate.

271
00:12:09,130 --> 00:12:10,200
Time flies, huh?

272
00:12:10,340 --> 00:12:11,990
You're already a PhD graduate.

273
00:12:11,990 --> 00:12:12,390
Yes.

274
00:12:13,890 --> 00:12:14,940
Come on, sit down.

275
00:12:15,180 --> 00:12:15,820
Don't just stand there.

276
00:12:15,820 --> 00:12:16,820
Have a seat.

277
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:18,130
Sit down now.

278
00:12:19,850 --> 00:12:20,490
Yizhong,

279
00:12:20,820 --> 00:12:22,490
now that you've got your doctorate,

280
00:12:22,490 --> 00:12:23,220
What's

281
00:12:23,610 --> 00:12:24,540
your plan next?

282
00:12:24,730 --> 00:12:27,130
I've been assigned
to the Academy of Social Sciences,

283
00:12:27,130 --> 00:12:28,460
at the Institute of Law.

284
00:12:28,470 --> 00:12:29,870
I've also passed

285
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:30,720
the bar exam.

286
00:12:31,070 --> 00:12:32,760
I'm thinking of taking on some

287
00:12:32,990 --> 00:12:34,190
part-time legal work
with Lawyer Yuan Yifang,

288
00:12:34,190 --> 00:12:35,650
if the opportunity comes.

289
00:12:35,750 --> 00:12:36,720
Let's celebrate.

290
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:38,450
You're going to be a lawyer too?

291
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:40,490
Wait, Cheng Jianji,

292
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:42,300
how did you teach your students?

293
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:42,970
Why is every single one of them

294
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:43,770
going astray?

295
00:12:44,370 --> 00:12:45,460
First Lu Zeming,

296
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:46,580
now you're dragging him

297
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:47,240
into it too?

298
00:12:47,940 --> 00:12:49,540
Zhou, I really don't like

299
00:12:50,250 --> 00:12:50,890
what you're saying.

300
00:12:50,890 --> 00:12:51,940
Like it or not.

301
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,790
What's wrong with

302
00:12:54,250 --> 00:12:55,420
