303
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:56,890
Do you need a PhD to be a lawyer?

304
00:12:56,890 --> 00:12:58,060
Count how many legal PhDs

305
00:12:58,060 --> 00:12:59,570
there are in the whole country.

306
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:00,560
You should be putting him

307
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:02,620
to work on something more important.

308
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:06,180
Yizhong.

309
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:08,580
The National People's Congress
is currently

310
00:13:08,580 --> 00:13:09,890
overhauling the 1979 Criminal Law

311
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:11,490
and Criminal Procedure Law.

312
00:13:12,070 --> 00:13:13,000
And I,

313
00:13:15,220 --> 00:13:16,900
along with this old fossil here,

314
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:18,560
are both on the revision team.

315
00:13:18,700 --> 00:13:19,730
Join us.

316
00:13:20,130 --> 00:13:21,530
Forget the lawyer thing.

317
00:13:23,250 --> 00:13:25,370
If you don't have a deeper,

318
00:13:25,540 --> 00:13:26,580
more comprehensive

319
00:13:26,580 --> 00:13:29,540
understanding of
the current state of the law,

320
00:13:30,610 --> 00:13:33,340
you're not qualified
to participate in law revision.

321
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:34,180
The revision process itself

322
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:35,100
is a learning process.

323
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:35,650
No, no.

324
00:13:35,650 --> 00:13:36,610
I think

325
00:13:36,630 --> 00:13:38,580
doing part-time legal work

326
00:13:38,850 --> 00:13:39,850
is exactly

327
00:13:39,850 --> 00:13:41,340
the kind of learning experience he needs.

328
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:42,600
So is revising the law!

329
00:13:42,620 --> 00:13:43,010
Yizhong-

330
00:13:43,010 --> 00:13:43,650
Mentors,

331
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:47,190
I'm happy to do whatever I'm needed for.

332
00:13:47,730 --> 00:13:48,890
If either of you needs me,

333
00:13:48,890 --> 00:13:50,490
just call and I'll come back.

334
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:51,970
Come on, cheers.

335
00:13:52,580 --> 00:13:53,550
Let's celebrate. Cheers.

336
00:13:53,550 --> 00:13:55,120
Who's celebrating with you?

337
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:55,950
Come on, cheers.

338
00:13:55,950 --> 00:13:56,480
Yizhong.

339
00:13:59,930 --> 00:14:03,910
[Beijing Station]

340
00:14:06,340 --> 00:14:06,890
You didn't go

341
00:14:06,890 --> 00:14:08,290
visit Mr. Zhou this time?

342
00:14:08,330 --> 00:14:09,750
He's been talking about you.

343
00:14:09,750 --> 00:14:11,110
No, I didn't dare.

344
00:14:11,470 --> 00:14:13,860
I was afraid Mrs. Zhou
wouldn't let me leave.

345
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:14,830
I was supposed to head back

346
00:14:14,830 --> 00:14:15,850
right after the meeting anyway.

347
00:14:15,850 --> 00:14:17,510
I already stayed an extra day.

348
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:21,220
It's been what,

349
00:14:21,220 --> 00:14:23,150
five or six years since we last met?

350
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:28,370
The four of us

351
00:14:28,880 --> 00:14:30,240
are drifting further apart.

352
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,630
I'm the one who's drifting.

353
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:34,700
You don't see

354
00:14:34,850 --> 00:14:36,180
the others much either?

355
00:14:37,940 --> 00:14:39,250
I see Lu often.

356
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:42,080
Yu Gaoyuan and Xia Yingjie—

357
00:14:43,060 --> 00:14:44,060
not so much.

358
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:47,270
You don't see Yingjie much either?

359
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:50,070
Last time we met

360
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:52,360
was over two years ago.

361
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:55,430
Is she still single?

362
00:14:55,980 --> 00:14:56,710
I don't know.

363
00:14:57,150 --> 00:14:57,820
I hope so.

364
00:15:02,170 --> 00:15:02,840
See?

365
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:04,660
Your real feelings are showing.

366
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:06,400
Honestly, you deserve it.

367
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:07,960
Let me remind you,

368
00:15:08,460 --> 00:15:09,980
whatever the reason,

369
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:11,340
if you keep being

370
00:15:11,370 --> 00:15:12,180
this passive,

371
00:15:12,610 --> 00:15:14,000
no one's going to wait for you

372
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:14,550
forever.

373
00:15:15,070 --> 00:15:16,500
Don't be so selfish.

374
00:15:19,540 --> 00:15:21,540
Make the first move. You're the guy.

375
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:27,600
Do you think I could

376
00:15:28,670 --> 00:15:30,240
go see Xu Zhaoyang?

377
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:33,600
You know it's not possible.

378
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:34,370
Why even ask?

379
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:37,190
If you hadn't urged them this time,

380
00:15:37,220 --> 00:15:38,540
who would have known that Xu Zhaoyang

381
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:40,940
is the same person
as Xu Zhao from back then?

382
00:15:41,970 --> 00:15:43,250
He's the most

383
00:15:43,460 --> 00:15:45,390
composed criminal I've ever seen—

384
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:46,810
emotionally stable,

385
00:15:46,810 --> 00:15:48,670
logically tight, tight-lipped.

386
00:15:48,890 --> 00:15:49,890
Xue Chunyan's case

387
00:15:49,890 --> 00:15:50,850
was years ago.

388
00:15:51,050 --> 00:15:52,650
Whether Xu Zhao was involved

389
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:54,660
still needs investigation.

390
00:15:54,950 --> 00:15:56,190
This isn't the first time

391
00:15:56,190 --> 00:15:58,030
he's had a relationship with a student.

392
00:15:58,030 --> 00:15:59,130
And you said it yourself.

393
00:15:59,130 --> 00:16:00,590
He could kill his own lover

394
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:01,730
and stay so calm,

395
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:02,540
so steady.

396
00:16:02,870 --> 00:16:04,650
He's probably done this before.

397
00:16:04,650 --> 00:16:06,010
You've studied criminal psychology,

398
00:16:06,010 --> 00:16:06,770
You know this type-

399
00:16:06,770 --> 00:16:08,570
But psychology isn't evidence.

400
00:16:17,570 --> 00:16:18,180
Yizhong,

401
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:20,170
I get how you feel.

402
00:16:21,170 --> 00:16:22,250
But Du Xiaohui

403
00:16:22,270 --> 00:16:24,000
was executed over a decade ago.

404
00:16:24,790 --> 00:16:26,310
You've worked in the system.

405
00:16:26,310 --> 00:16:27,710
You know how hard this is.

406
00:16:29,130 --> 00:16:30,460
Attention passengers,

407
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:33,820
Train 427 to Linshan

408
00:16:33,970 --> 00:16:35,370
is now boarding.

409
00:16:35,650 --> 00:16:36,250
Let's go.

410
00:16:36,350 --> 00:16:37,940
Remember to call Yingjie.

411
00:16:38,310 --> 00:16:39,010
Even if you can't see her,

412
00:16:39,010 --> 00:16:41,340
hearing her voice is better than nothing.

413
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:42,360
Give it to me.

414
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:44,020
Let me. It's fine. I've got it.

415
00:17:03,090 --> 00:17:05,349
Why are there so many armed police today?

416
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:07,760
They're transferred from the south.

417
00:17:08,140 --> 00:17:09,540
All serving life or more.

418
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:12,740
Everyone off the bus!

419
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:13,990
Be prepared.

420
00:17:14,849 --> 00:17:16,450
These inmates are the hardest to handle.

421
00:17:16,450 --> 00:17:17,760
Hurry, line up over there!

422
00:17:17,760 --> 00:17:20,140
They were transferred
from the south to here all of a sudden.

423
00:17:20,140 --> 00:17:21,940
The environment change is huge.

424
00:17:22,190 --> 00:17:22,859
When...

425
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:23,490
Hurry up.

426
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:25,380
people get desperate,

427
00:17:26,470 --> 00:17:28,329
you never know what they might do.

428
00:17:28,930 --> 00:17:29,780
Hurry up.

429
00:17:30,850 --> 00:17:31,580
Move faster.

430
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:32,100
Faster.

431
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:33,740
Line up.

432
00:17:34,560 --> 00:17:35,320
That guy

433
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:37,180
seems to have knee problems.

434
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:39,060
We should get a doctor
to check him out later.

435
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:39,690
Line up!

436
00:17:42,860 --> 00:17:43,580
Hurry up.

437
00:17:45,930 --> 00:17:46,740
Yan Jicai, get off.

438
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:47,290
Get off!

439
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:48,630
-I'm innocent!
-Get off.

440
00:17:48,630 --> 00:17:49,610
I'm innocent! I didn't kill anyone!

441
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:50,780
Get off! Yan Jicai!

442
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:51,930
I'm innocent! I didn't kill anyone!

443
00:17:51,930 --> 00:17:52,610
-Get off!
-No, I won’t!

444
00:17:52,610 --> 00:17:53,130
Get off!

445
00:17:54,690 --> 00:17:56,450
I'm not getting off!

446
00:17:56,470 --> 00:17:58,000
Get down! Behave yourself!

447
00:17:59,540 --> 00:18:00,280
How many like this

448
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:01,350
are in this batch?

449
00:18:02,260 --> 00:18:03,390
Just this one so far.

450
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:06,230
When you get one like this,

451
00:18:06,230 --> 00:18:08,230
the trouble's only just beginning.

452
00:18:08,580 --> 00:18:08,980
Let go of me!

453
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:10,110
I'm not getting off!

454
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:11,370
Get down here!

455
00:18:11,370 --> 00:18:12,170
I'm innocent!

456
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:13,130
I'm innocent!

457
00:18:13,130 --> 00:18:13,690
Behave yourself!

458
00:18:13,690 --> 00:18:14,610
I didn't kill anyone!

459
00:18:14,610 --> 00:18:15,610
Behave yourself!

460
00:18:15,650 --> 00:18:16,330
Behave!

461
00:18:16,450 --> 00:18:17,580
Why should I get off?

462
00:18:17,720 --> 00:18:18,520
I'm innocent!

463
00:18:18,850 --> 00:18:20,450
-Don’t move.
-I’m innocent.

464
00:18:21,930 --> 00:18:23,020
I'm innocent!

465
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:24,380
I didn't kill anyone!

466
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:25,820
I didn't kill anyone!

467
00:18:32,380 --> 00:18:34,580
I'm innocent!

468
00:18:38,170 --> 00:18:41,040
[Criminal File Transfer]

469
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:40,320
The guy who was yelling just now

470
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:41,350
is Yan Jicai.

471
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:43,580
He's been making a scene
since he got here.

472
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:44,130
I've never seen

473
00:18:44,130 --> 00:18:45,540
behavior like that.

474
00:18:47,170 --> 00:18:48,690
I've seen it before.

475
00:18:51,410 --> 00:18:52,410
People like that—

476
00:18:52,820 --> 00:18:53,450
they

477
00:18:53,930 --> 00:18:54,890
genuinely

478
00:18:54,890 --> 00:18:56,820
don't believe they did it.

479
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:58,630
He's not lying, really.

480
00:18:58,890 --> 00:19:00,020
There's this

481
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:01,980
little voice in his head,

482
00:19:02,790 --> 00:19:04,040
